overview": "Virginia's 1st District is one of the most closely watched House races of 2026, with Republican incumbent Rob Wittman defending a seat that only narrowly favors his party against Democratic challenger Shannon Taylor. Wittman has a large financial edge, with about $4.3 million on hand to Taylor's $1 million, though outside groups have spent against him. Rating outlets are divided: several call the race Lean R, others Tossup, and one rates it a Democratic flip opportunity.\n\nThe only recent poll, a Democratic internal from mid-September, shows a one-point race, and prediction markets give Taylor roughly a 40% chance of winning. With the House majority potentially running through Virginia, both parties are investing heavily, and the race sits right at the tossup line with a slight Republican tilt.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.4506, "margin": -0.72}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.4359, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.4341, "margin": -1.5}]}